WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:11.060
Ah, love.

00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:15.560
You gotta love it. Everywhere you look, there
it is.

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:22.370
But in the city that never sleeps. How do you
really know who the hell you're sleeping with?

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:25.310
People can conceal some very dirty secrets.

00:00:29.390 --> 00:00:31.880
Or fatally fatal flaws.

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:38.240
Everything's fine.

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:40.700
Joy is just loudly shattering sea glass to put in
her aquarium.

00:00:40.730 --> 00:00:42.180
Sure, sure. Sure.

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:47.420
Uhh, have you asked your new fiance about the lipstick yet?
Did she write "f*cking pig" on Ben's dressing room mirror?

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:49.910
Yeah. No, but I will.

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:53.550
Charles, you said you would ask her two days
ago. Let us in. We could talk to her.

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:56.750
I am handling the situation in my own time.

00:00:56.780 --> 00:00:59.150
See, I told you he didn't need our help, but

00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:03.440
I do. Does this scarf say "Loretta, I've loved
you since the first day I met you"?

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:06.950
I don't know what the scarf is saying, but
all I could see is a crayon box.

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:12.140
Oh, well, see, that's why we always carry a
backup. Thank you, Mabel.

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:17.420
Charles, I can calmly talk to Joy, you know,
investigator woman to suspect woman.

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:23.120
She is not another Jan. Well, she could be.
But it's important for me to be able to

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:27.260
interrogate my murderous girlfriend... Fiance?
Shit.

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:32.090
What about my hair? Is it giving Karen or
Cary Grant?

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:35.840
Hold on, Mabel Mora...

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:37.520
Are you going out on a date?

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:37.530
Date?

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:42.350
No, no, no, Tobert has a suspect he has a lead on.

00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:45.170
I'm meeting him for a stakeout, and the place has a dress code.

00:01:46.070 --> 00:01:47.270
Well, it's a date.

00:01:47.390 --> 00:01:47.930
Yeah.

00:01:47.930 --> 00:01:52.250
It's a stakeout. When two totally
platonic, semi-professional investigators

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:57.110
wait together in an out-of-sight enclosed
space and watch while a suspect hopefully

00:01:57.110 --> 00:02:01.850
incriminates themselves while we hold in our
pee for hours and eat stale Cheetos.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:03.500
In a cocktail dress.

00:02:03.820 --> 00:02:08.060
Look, I'm gonna unmute your text. I'll be in
the wings if anything should go haywire.

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:11.330
I'll be okay.

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:25.700
Is it possible you're sleeping next to a
lunatic or a liar? Sure it is. But I always

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:29.780
tell people, better lose your mind loving
than to live your life loveless.

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:35.150
It's been a while since I dipped my quill in
a woman's ink pot. Any new moves I should

00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:35.900
know about?

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:38.510
Please don't make me take the next one.

